      "content": "For the corner with the hot tub, you'll need to account for the increased load from the hot tub itself, as well as the distribution of loads from the surrounding joists. This is often referred to as the \"deck edge\" or \"corner load.\" You can use an additional multiplier of 1.5, typically recommended by the IRC, to account for these concentrated loads. When using this method, you would need to apply the heavy loads from the surrounding joists to the corner height of the joist above. Alternatively, consult a more detailed load calculation, or consult a deck-building professional for the specifics.",
